cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ìlànà: a software engineering process operating system for coding agents"
message: "If you use Ìlànà in research or teaching, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Ìlànà contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ferousco-dev/ilana"
url: "https://github.com/Ferousco-dev/ilana"
abstract: >-
  Ìlànà is a gated software engineering process definition for AI coding agents. It
  implements eleven lifecycle phases, nine quality gates with criteria scaled by a
  five-level rigour dial, thirteen specialist agent roles with enforced separation of
  duties, ten cross-phase protocols, and a set of dependency-free measurement
  instruments. It is derived from SEN102/212 Software Engineering Process at Obafemi
  Awolowo University, Ile-Ife, and aligns with ISO/IEC 12207, IEEE 830, IEEE 1016,
  IEEE 829, CMMI and the ACM/IEEE Software Engineering Code of Ethics. It is
  host-agnostic and ships adapters for Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Cursor, Windsurf,
  Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, Continue, Aider and OpenCode.
keywords:
  - software engineering
  - software process
  - requirements engineering
  - software testing
  - software quality assurance
  - software configuration management
  - process improvement
  - CMMI
  - ISO/IEC 12207
  - AI coding agents
  - agent skills
  - software engineering education
license: MIT
